{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>The barn owl.</b> All who see it are astonished. This name is also found among the creeping things." "<b>The vomiter.</b> Some say there is a bird whose nature is to regurgitate its food." "<b>The raham.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] said that it is in the language of Kedar, by interchange of ḥet and kaf, for in their script they are one letter. And others said that it is a bird that has compassion on its young."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:27.687927360Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}